# Copy this file to `.env` for local development.
#
# This file is committed, so every value in it is a placeholder. Real secrets
# belong in `.env.local`, which is gitignored and overrides every value here.
# See DATABASE.md, "Where Credentials Go".

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres, hosted at Neon. There is no local-file fallback any more: the app
# throws at startup if this is unset rather than half-working against an empty
# default. Pull the real string with `stripe projects env --pull`, or copy it
# from the Neon dashboard.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# ── Contact-form delivery ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these the form still works — notes are saved and readable in the
# database — they just do not get emailed. `app/lib/sendNotification.ts` is the
# only module that reads them.

# Sending goes through Customer.io's transactional API, authenticated with the
# sandbox service-account token Stripe Projects provisions. It is already in
# `.env` — not listed here — written by:
#     stripe projects add customerio/builder:sandbox
#     stripe projects variables set customerio-send-token \
#       --env-key CUSTOMERIO_SEND_TOKEN --value <the NADIA_MAIL_SA_TOKEN value>
# The second command is what gives it this stable name; the raw variable is
# NADIA_MAIL_*, whose prefix comes from the resource's `--name`.
#
# Note the NADIA_MAIL_SITE_ID / NADIA_MAIL_API_KEY pair is for the Track API,
# not for sending. It will authenticate against track.customer.io and fail here.

# Set to `eu` if the Customer.io workspace is in the European region. The
# regional hosts are separate deployments and a key issued in one is rejected
# by the other. Unset means US — which is what this workspace reported.
CUSTOMERIO_REGION=""

# Where notes are delivered. NEVER put the real address in this file — it is
# committed, and the whole point of routing through the form is that the
# address is not published anywhere. Real value goes in `.env.local` only.
CONTACT_INBOX=""

# The From: address notes are sent as. Must be on a domain verified with the
# mail provider, otherwise delivery is rejected. This one is public by nature —
# it appears in the header of every notification.
#
# On the sandbox tier this MUST be the workspace's assigned sending domain,
# which looks like `hello@<words>.us.customerio.build`. A nadiaeldeib.com
# sender only works once that domain is verified in Customer.io (DNS records),
# which is deploy-cycle work — see REBUILD_PLAN.md.
CONTACT_FROM=""
